nodecode-gmi-image is a rewrite of zkasuran's zkasuran/hermes-gmi-media:
https://github.com/zkasuran/hermes-gmi-media
commit 6760b29d6f9f93f47cef08702bda876fb10af652

Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) zkasuran (LICENSE names no holder)

What was rewritten: the plugin's one image backend (__init__.py, gmi_media.py)
became a Nodecode cell in Common Lisp. Kept from it: the requestqueue base URL
and its three routes (models, models/<id>, requests and requests/<id>), the
bearer key read from the environment and scrubbed out of every error text, the
model schema read whole - parameters with their options, bounds and defaults,
input and output modalities, qworkers, visibility and pricing - the payload
mapped onto the parameters a model declares (prompt to prompt or text, the
named aspect to aspect_ratio, else the nearest offered size under the plugin's
2048x2048 ceiling), the one-hour schema cache, the preference order
seedream-5.0-lite, gemini-2.5-flash-image, gpt-image-2-generate, the rule that
a model needing a source picture is only picked for an edit, image inputs as
public http(s) URLs only and at most three, the submit-then-poll job with its
growing delay and its deadline, the outcome's media URL order including the
thumbnail fallback, the 429 handling that tells a daily model limit from a
burst, the price text, and the picture fetched at once because GMI's link may
expire.

What was left out, and why: plugin.yaml, the Hermes provider registration and
the ImageGenProvider class, the picker and setup-schema methods, and the
per-request environment lookup, none of which exist outside that runtime - here
the cell declares one section, one tool (gmi_image) and one command
(/gmi-image), and reads the key once at start. The full catalog read - every
model's schema at once, for a picker - is left out with the picker: a call
reads only the schema of the model it will use, in the order the plugin's own
cold-start probe used. The audio download helper and the video and audio
concepts in the payload mapper are left out because this cell draws images
only.
